WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.523
As the pirates had discovered, there was no visible entrance to the boys' underground home.

2
00:00:06.524 --> 00:00:10.652
Instead, there were seven separate doors.

3
00:00:10.653 --> 00:00:18.515
Seven hollow trees acted as tunnels. The tunnels fit each Lost Boy exactly.

4
00:00:18.516 --> 00:00:24.723
Each tree was the exact size of each boy, so they could easily slide in and out.

5
00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:32.426
Peter measured Wendy, John, and Michael, so that they too could have their own hollow tree entrances.

6
00:00:32.427 --> 00:00:37.515
Unless the fit was perfect, it was difficult to slide up and down.

7
00:00:37.516 --> 00:00:44.311
Peter taught them to draw in their breath, and then wriggle down the hollow at just the right speed.

8
00:00:44.312 --> 00:00:47.099
Coming back up was much the same.

9
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.440
After a few days' practice, they were going up and down easily.

10
00:00:52.441 --> 00:00:57.436
Rough and simple, the underground home was little more than a cave.

11
00:00:57.437 --> 00:01:01.338
It was mostly one large room with a dirt floor.

12
00:01:01.339 --> 00:01:05.081
A huge fireplace stood in the middle of the room.

13
00:01:05.082 --> 00:01:09.001
The fire could be seen from anywhere in the room.

14
00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:15.288
Big fat mushrooms served as stools. A tree grew in one corner of the room.

15
00:01:15.289 --> 00:01:18.881
The boys sawed it down to floor level every morning.

16
00:01:18.882 --> 00:01:23.297
But every afternoon it grew about two feet high.

17
00:01:23.298 --> 00:01:27.751
They covered it with a door, and this served as their table.

18
00:01:27.752 --> 00:01:34.766
After supper, they would clear the table, take down the door, and saw off the trunk again.

19
00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:40.110
This way, they had more room to play and dance in the evenings.

20
00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:46.033
A great big bed was tilted against the wall by day and set down at night.

21
00:01:46.034 --> 00:01:48.862
It filled nearly half the room.

22
00:01:48.863 --> 00:01:55.463
All the boys, except Michael, slept together and squished like sardines in a can.

23
00:01:55.464 --> 00:01:58.881
When one rolled over, they all rolled over.

24
00:01:58.882 --> 00:02:04.844
Michael was the youngest, so Wendy decided to hang a basket up for his bed.

25
00:02:04.845 --> 00:02:08.436
It was hard taking care of nine active boys.

26
00:02:08.437 --> 00:02:11.417
Every day Wendy cooked for them.

27
00:02:11.418 --> 00:02:15.999
Sometimes it was real food collected by the boys during the day.

28
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.981
Other times it was make-believe food, which they enjoyed almost as much.

29
00:02:21.982 --> 00:02:25.690
She cleaned the house and washed their clothes.

30
00:02:25.691 --> 00:02:29.944
At night, she tucked the boys in and told them a story.

31
00:02:29.945 --> 00:02:33.048
Wendy was very strict about bedtime.

32
00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:38.144
All the boys had to be in bed by seven in the evening.

33
00:02:38.145 --> 00:02:42.741
After the boys had gone to sleep, she sewed new things for them.

34
00:02:42.742 --> 00:02:46.826
She patched the knees in their pants and darned their socks.

35
00:02:46.827 --> 00:02:49.950
It was a very busy life for Wendy.

36
00:02:49.951 --> 00:02:55.101
She loved to be needed, and she loved her underground life with the boys.

37
00:02:55.102 --> 00:03:00.198
The only thing that bothered her was that Tinker Bell did not approve of her.

38
00:03:00.199 --> 00:03:03.652
Tinker Bell lived in the underground house too.

39
00:03:03.653 --> 00:03:07.618
She had her own special spot in a nook in the wall.

40
00:03:07.619 --> 00:03:12.928
No larger than a birdcage, this was Tinker Bell's own private place.

41
00:03:12.929 --> 00:03:17.518
Unlike the messy boys, Tink was very neat and clean.

42
00:03:17.519 --> 00:03:20.820
She didn't need a mother to take care of her.

43
00:03:20.821 --> 00:03:26.973
No girl, large or small, had a lovelier bedroom than Tinker Bell.

44
00:03:26.974 --> 00:03:32.895
Each season, she changed her bedspread to match the colors of the trees and flowers.

45
00:03:32.896 --> 00:03:37.318
Her curtains were made of the finest butterfly wings.

46
00:03:37.319 --> 00:03:42.282
She always drew her tiny curtains when she was dressing or undressing.

47
00:03:42.283 --> 00:03:47.474
Everyone was very happy to have Wendy around, but not Tinker Bell.

48
00:03:47.475 --> 00:03:51.194
Sometimes the fairy kept her anger to herself.

49
00:03:51.195 --> 00:03:55.595
Other times Tinker Bell plotted against Wendy.

50
00:03:55.596 --> 00:04:05.727
One night Tinker Bell tried, with the help of some fairy friends, to float the sleeping Wendy on a great big leaf back to the mainland.

51
00:04:05.728 --> 00:04:11.468
Fortunately, the leaf gave way and Wendy woke up just in time.

52
00:04:11.469 --> 00:04:18.319
She fell into the water and swam back.

